On Thu, 5 Sep 2024, Elena wrote:
> After upgrading the toolchain the ARM build stops with an "undefined
> reference" error in the linker step. x86 is fine.

I hit the same thing last week. The new compiler enables link-time
optimisation by default, and our ARM linker script drops one of the
sections it needs. Passing -fno-lto in the ARM toolchain file fixes it
for now.

I opened an issue with a minimal reproduction and attached the full
build log. A proper fix is probably to update the linker script, but I
haven't had time to test that on real hardware yet.

Tomasz
